{"id": "EUVD-2026-103579", "enisaUuid": "4ff74e71-5650-3e5c-9d69-632bb8c3f242", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipe: fix use-after-free when auditing a newly loaded policy\n\nnew_policy() audits the policy after ipe_new_policyfs_node() publishes it\nand drops the new directory's inode lock. A concurrent delete can free\nthe policy while ipe_audit_policy_load() is still using it.\n\nAudit the successful load under that lock.\n\n[FW: remove model name according to latest guideline]", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b72d6c72b4bfbc021e8e127fa13e0f27d09be737", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/48f7d0233c3cc8d986d1177d0e5dd4af435e7265", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9015d32752fa228ef2f0e07fd93fc53a4a4c723", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9814077275eca36ebf8d510d2f076d235ff9f51a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98534", "GHSA-rvjx-cgvf-j557"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1395fcf0-1665-310a-b295-02bff18b3e52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "258a55b8-1e35-35fd-8d40-6ee81f41f4ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "2768ff20-4ee1-3e8f-941e-b93830e59721", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f44554b5067b36c14cc91ed811fa1bd58baed34a <48f7d0233c3cc8d986d1177d0e5dd4af435e7265"}, {"id": "31d141aa-6878-32b3-9cfc-0131d4462322", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "4d4cf532-135c-36a1-966f-84859c74a88b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "523c457a-6683-3028-b059-0807d53148a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "73c985b5-d2